title: SecondLoopFabian1
tags:
---
NARRATOR: The muted streets of Solster are before you, again. 
NARRATOR: The square before the train station is faded, empty, and an absolutely miraculous sight to see. 
NARRATOR: The void that just consumed the town moments before now lingers only in your mind. 
NARRATOR: The town before you is intact, lit by the low light of the Everwatcher’s light on the sky. 
NARRATOR: The same light you saw mere hours before, when you stepped out of the train station, for the first time. What in the world is going on?

-> “I’ve gone insane. I lost my mind. This cannot be real”
-> “I guess that must have been a dream… A very uncannily realistic dream.”
-> “I’m suffering from delusions, possibly a symptom of stress and poor sleeping. I have no prior history of hallucinations, so it must be a one-time circumstantial event” << if $PsychMajor == true >>
-> “I imagined a story in which Solster met its end by the hand of the consuming void. My imagination is too strong for my own good clearly, so I pictured it so vividly I actually believed it was real” << if $ArtMajor == true >>
-> “The train was poorly ventilated, clearly. I think I could smell some smoke from the engine in my compartment at some point. This hallucination was caused by light oxygen deprivation during the trip. Lucky that it didn’t get worse than this.” << if $TechMajor == true >>

NARRATOR: There is just one person in sight of you on the square. 
NARRATOR: Not your brother. A young peppy man, no older than 30. 
NARRATOR: A man you have never met before.
NARRATOR: He smiles and waves cheerfully at you, as if his entire world had not just ended minutes ago.

-> “Fabian?”
    SASHA: “Fabian?”
    FABIAN: (surprised) Oh, you already knew my name? I didn’t realise Dmitriy had told you I’d be here to pick you up! 
    FABIAN: That's me! Fabian Goldhirsch, the, uhm, new youth pastor. 
    FABIAN: It’s a pleasure to meet you, Sasha! (extends his hand for a handshake)
-> “Are you okay? How… How are we still alive?”
    SASHA: “Are you okay? How… How are we still alive?”
    FABIAN: (short silence) Oh, I mean yeah, I’m perfectly fine. Alfonz is the one who… Well, yes, I am still alive and kicking, as they say.
    FABIAN: I am Fabian Goldhirsch, the new youth pastor as you seem to have surmised.  (trails off awkwardly)
    FABIAN: I came here to greet you at the station, and I’m quite happy to meet you Sasha! (extends his hand for a handshake)
-> “What the fuck is going on? Why are we here?”
    SASHA: “What the fuck is going on? Why are we here?”
    FABIAN: Oh, I’m sorry… I know I’m not who you were expecting. (mutter) though that was rather..
    FABIAN: I’m Fabian Goldhirsch, the youth pastor. The, uhm, new youth pastor.
    FABIAN: Your brother couldn’t make it here, unfortunately, so he asked me to come greet you at the station. 
    FABIAN: Regardless of circumstance, I’m happy to make your acquaintance, Sasha. (extends his hand for a handshake)
	
	
-> Shake his hand
	SASHA: (shakes his hand)
	FABIAN: “Are you okay Sasha? Your hand is so shaky.”
-> “The world just ended. We all died.”
	FABIAN: I… Are you okay Sasha? 
	FABIAN: The world is still here and we are all very much alive. I don’t really understand what you are talking about.
-> “Didn’t we already meet a few hours ago? We’ve been through this before.”
    FABIAN: (confused smile) I’m quite sure this is our first time ever meeting. I’m sure I’d have remembered meeting someone like you!
-> “I… I think I need some space right now. I don’t know what is going on.”
	FABIAN: Oh, I’m sorry to hear that Sasha. Are you feeling okay?
	FABIAN: What’s got you so troubled?


-> “I am okay, yeah… I’m just a bit shaken by the trip”
	FABIAN: I’m sure it is just fatigue. I know I was a little clumsy after getting out of the train when I arrived here as well.
	FABIAN: If you want, you could pass by the Star and get yourself checked out. That way you can be fully reassured everything is a-okay with you!
	NARRATOR: The Star Hospital, the only hospital Solster has to offer. 
	NARRATOR: You have some unpleasant memories of it, but not any that are particularly out of the ordinary for a hospital.
	NARRATOR: But Star doesn't offer children any compensatory candy, which has truly sullied the experience.
-> “I don’t think I’m feeling too well…”
	FABIAN: I’m sorry to hear that, that is some unlucky timing
	FABIAN: Do you think you might be sick? Maybe disoriented from the trip?
	FABIAN: If you want, you could head over to the Star, get yourself checked out there. I’m sure the doctors there can help.
	NARRATOR: The Star Hospital, the only hospital Solster has to offer. 
	NARRATOR: You have some unpleasant memories of it, but not any that are particularly out of the ordinary for a hospital.
	NARRATOR: But Star doesn't offer children any compensatory candy, which has truly sullied the experience.
-> “No, I am not even remotely okay. I have already been here, and I died, and you died, and now I am back here again. I feel like I am in hell.”
	SASHA: “No, I am not even remotely okay. I have already been here, and I died, and you died, and now I am back here again. I feel like I am in hell.”
	SASHA: “How can you not remember that? You were there! We went to the parade, we got to the end, and the darkness started coming over all of us!”
	SASHA: “It swarmed the whole town, everything was dark, it was so cold, and painful, and I tried to scream and nothing came out, and and”
	SASHA: “I… This is impossible. We should be dead. We are dead right now. But we are back to this morning. Please tell me you remember it too. Please.”
	FABIAN: (has since backed away slightly) Sasha, nothing has happened. Everything is okay here, we are all alive and well
	FABIAN: I… don’t know what you are feeling right now, but whatever happened to you must have been really upsetting.
	FABIAN: It’s okay to vent out your feelings, but you don’t need to shout, please.
	FABIAN: Maybe you should try going to the Star? If you are feeling unwell, the doctors there could help.
	NARRATOR: The Star Hospital, the only hospital Solster has to offer. 
	NARRATOR: While you are unsure of their medical treatment of "doomsday loop", it's worth a shot.
	
	
//After Fabian tells you about the star
-> “I’m going to go to the Star hospital now, then. We can talk later.”
	FABIAN: That sounds like a great idea. Do you remember where the Hospital is? Just head south-east from here, there’s no missing it.
	FABIAN: I’ll be heading to the parade later, if you need me. I take it that I’ll see you there later?
	FABIAN: (about to leave) Oh right, and before I forget, your brother is working setting up the parade. If you want to talk to him, you can find him there!
-> “I need to talk to Dmitriy. Or anyone else. I think I am losing my mind here.”
	FABIAN: I… I see. I understand, yes. It’s been a long trip for you, it makes sense you want to see your brother first.
	FABIAN: Your brother should be still working on setting up the parade. 
	FABIAN: I hope you can find him quickly. I’ll talk to you later, Sasha.
-> “I am getting out of here, right now. I don’t want to die again.”
	NARRATOR:You are not going to die here, especially not right after finishing college. You refuse to.
	NARRATOR: You turn around to look at the timetable, and are met with a grim sight. A simple piece of paper, attached to the table, likely just before you arrived, with an announcement.
	NARRATOR: ‘Due to today’s festivities, the regular 16:00 train out of Solster shall depart tomorrow at 11:30 instead.’
    FABIAN: (talking, unheard) …And it would be a shame for your brother, wouldn’t it be?
    FABIAN: …Sasha? Are you still with me?
    FABIAN: (exhausted irritation) I really think you should go to a doctor. If you can excuse me saying this, something seems not right with you.
    FABIAN: I mean I have never met you before, but this does not seem like how I’d expect you to act from what Dmitriy had told me of you.
    -> “I’m sorry.”
	    FABIAN: (nods tersely) It’s okay, Sasha. I understand you must still be feeling quite stressed, with so many big things happening lately. Alfonz, moving back to Solster, finishing your study…
	    FABIAN: I hope that you will find some calm in the coming days. If I can help in any way, you can always come to talk to me.
    -> Leave without a word.

===
